## Ported, and altered

The scenes under `<name>/src/net/b12n/raylib_ios/scenes/` are ports of examples
that now live in jlt-commons/raylib-jolt-demo, which kept the raylib-jlt
examples when raylib-jlt became a library. Each is an altered version: the loop
is inverted so the host owns it, geometry derives from the live screen instead
of a fixed 800x450, randomness becomes a seeded LCG, and drawing moves to the
caller. Every file names its original, as raylib-jolt-demo's demo with
"originally raylib-jlt", in its own docstring, as the zlib licence's "altered
source versions must be plainly marked as such" asks.

Which licence an original carries depends on when it was added to raylib-jlt.
That repository was zlib until its 2026-09-05 relicence and is EPL 2.0 after, so
a scene ported from an example added later is EPL 2.0 (Copyright (c) 2026 Burin
Choomnuan). Eight of the ten texture scenes (Source and Destination Rects,
Sprite Button, Npatch Drawing, Polygon Drawing, Sprite Animation, Textured
Curve, Raw Data and Screen Buffer) are EPL 2.0; only Texture Tiling and
Procedural Textures predate the relicence. The same holds for four of the five
render-target scenes (Framebuffer Rendering, Mouse Painting, Magnifying Glass
and Top Down Lights); Render Texture (2026-08-23) predates the relicence and is
zlib. Each of those docstrings gives its original's licence, and the raylib C
examples behind them are zlib, so their altered-source marking stands.

